2. ", "title": "Council Directive 93/13/EEC of 5 April 1993 on unfair terms in consumer contracts", "source_url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:31993L0013", "article_labels": ["Article 7"], "n": 3}, {"rank": 4, "score": 0.5683714747428894, "chunk_id": "874595564f061afa26aa83dbe0d6d598049bd1ca31d6fce734145cd622425536", "corpus_version": "794e3d1956fc324659da149d5bfb0e083d257845895057b631d4578ec5b29795", "condition": "s400", "document_id": "eu_unfair_terms_93_13", "article_ids": [], "start": 7365, "end": 7721, "text": "Whereas Member States should ensure that unfair terms are not used in contracts concluded with consumers by a seller or supplier and that if, nevertheless, such terms are so used, they will not bind the consumer, and the contract will continue to bind the parties upon those terms if it is capable of continuing in existence without the unfair provisions;
